      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='371' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='370' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98666' id='3' type-v2='text' w='64166' x='556' y='667'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#dd0000' fontsize='14'>Marketing Efficiency project description</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='12'>Goal: </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Identify the most efficient marketing campaign sources and support marketing optimisations by providing a standard vendor marketing efficiency score.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='12'>Description: </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>Each week vendor gets Score based on it&apos;s efficiency.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>The score vary from 1 to 5</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'> where 5 is the best score vendor could get.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>There are </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>5  KPIs </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='10'>that are currently selected for scoring.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>KPIs and their weights: </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>1. CVR diff -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> Difference between CVR on CPC campaigns and average vendor CVR. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Formula</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>:</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>CPC CVR - CVR. Only available for the vendors that do CPC.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Weight:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> 0.25</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>2. CPO euro - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Marketing spend from RDF, Gem, CPC and Vendor Discounts is divided by unique number of orders from these marketing channels to get to the cost per order. </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Formula</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>: (cpc_spend_eur + gem_spend_eur + rdf_spend_eur + discount_spend_eur)/ (unique orders from cpc, gem, rdf and vendor discounts)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Weight:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> 0.25</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>3. ROAS new -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Return on marketing spend for new users only (vendor level acquisitions are counted in). </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Revenue that vendor got from acquired customers is divided by the campaign spend.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Formula</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>(</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>cpc_gmv_eur_new + gem_gmv_eur_new + rdf_gmv_eur_new + discount_gmv_eur_new)/</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>(cpc_spend_eur + gem_spend_eur + rdf_spend_eur + discount_spend_eur)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Weight:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> 0.25</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>4. Spend GBV</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Marketing spend is divided by total vendor GBV to indicate what percentage of total basket value would be spent on Marketing. Depending on where the vendor stays in its lifecycle it could be a different number, but often a healthy number could be around 5%.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Formula</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>: (cpc_spend_eur + gem_spend_eur + rdf_spend_eur + discount_spend_eur)/gbv_eur</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Weight:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> 0.05</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>5. Acquisition Rate</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>This metric shows the share of new users that were acquired through marketing activities.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Formula</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>: Marketing  acquisitions/ Marketing unique orders</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Weight:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> 0.25</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>As the</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='12'> benchmark </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>are</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>taken results from platform vendors on 3 levels:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#dd0000' fontsize='10'>1 level</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>:  Entity, cuisine, vendor maturity , report week (Limitation: 10 vendors+ in the sample),</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#dd0000' fontsize='10'>2 level</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>: Entity, cuisine, report week (Limitation: 10 vendors+ in the sample),</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#dd0000' fontsize='10'>3 level</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>:  Entity, report week (applicable for all remaining vendors)</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='12'>Score</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>will be assigned to the vendor based on the following logics:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>CVR diff, Acquisition Rate</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>When, e.g., CVR diff for a vendor is within 0.5(half) standard deviation of CVR difference benchmark mean, then it gets score 3, that indicates good performance. When CVR diff for a vendor falls between half standard and full standard deviation, then score will be 2 or 4. Once the difference is bigger than 1 standard deviation than the scores will be 1 or 5 (see graph on top right).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4e79a7' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Good to know than appr. 68% of all data is located within 1 standard deviation of the mean.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>GBV Spend</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>,</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'> ROAS new</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> and </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>CPO new</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='11'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>are using instead of mean and standard deviation -  median and median deviation, due to long tail distribution.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>When the vendor metric is within 0.4 median deviation of median benchmark value than the score is 3, when it is between 0.4 and 0.9 median deviation then the score is 2 or 4. The score is 5 or 1 when deviation is bigger than 0.9 of median benchmark.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
